Hello

I'm sorry. I have downgraded R to 3.3.3 and my app work now normally so I can't reproduce the crash errors (I haven't got any development environment).

When I was using my shiny app with web browser from a client it simply write that the application has crashed and that information errors were sent to js console or something like that.
When I ran the app from R studio to debug, it simply crashed Rstudio (fatal error).

The app has multi tab and we have found 2 parts of the code which seems to be at the origin of the crash.

- First part calls a leaflet map with reactive points (addCircleMarkers). The tab with one specific map generate crash whereas other quite similar leaflet maps on other tabs worked normally.

- Second one make the app crashed after loading data and trying to display it with a plotly/ggplot (the data load normally but when the server try to display the graph, the app crash). We use other plotly / ggplot graphs in other part of the app without any problem.

Sorry for not being able to send a reproducible example.

Regards,

Anthony

