I'm struggling with a 2-sided Shiny problem and finding very little support on StackOverflow.

I need to implement a `ggvis` graphic with (a) a hover tooltip that displays a headline detail and (b) a click tooltip that sends content to a uiOutput panel.  I'm having problems (1) implementing click and hover tooltips together (the hover tooltip also kills the click tooltip on mouseoff <https://stackoverflow.com/questions/43986901/implementing-separate-hover-and-click-tooltips-with-ggvis>), and (2) getting the uiOutput panel to be properly reactive to a click tooltip <https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44045714/making-a-reactive-global-variable-in-shiny>.  For now I'd be more grateful for any assistance anyone can offer on the first of these:

Separate tooltips - demo code:

require(ggvis); require(shiny)

headline = function(x) "Now click on the point"
all_values = function(x) "<a href='http://google.com/'>I want to click here</a>"

server = function(input, output, session) {
  observe({
    ggvis(mtcars, ~disp, ~mpg) %>% layer_points() %>%
      add_tooltip(headline, 'hover') %>%
      add_tooltip(all_values, 'click') %>%
      bind_shiny('ggvis_plot', 'ggvis_ui')
  })
}

ui = fluidPage( uiOutput("ggvis_ui"), ggvisOutput("ggvis_plot"))
shinyApp(ui, server)

Thanks in advance.

